\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
\emph on
Want to show: 
\begin_inset Formula $x\succeq y$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is represented by 
\begin_inset Formula $u:X\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

, we have that 
\begin_inset Formula $u(x^{t})\ge u(y^{t})\ \forall\ t\in\mathbb{N}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since limits preserve weak inequalities, we have that 
\begin_inset Formula $\underset{t\to\infty}{\lim}\ u(x^{t})\geq\underset{t\to\infty}{\lim}\ u(y^{t})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 is a continuous function, then 
\begin_inset Formula $u(x^{t})\underset{t\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}u(x)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $u(y^{t})\underset{t\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}u(y)$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus, we have that 
\begin_inset Formula $u(x)\geq u(y)$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So, 
\begin_inset Formula $x\succeq y$
\end_inset

 since 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 represents 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Hence, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \{x^{t}\},\{y^{t}\}\subseteq X:\left[x^{t}\underset{t\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}x\land\; y^{t}\underset{t\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}y\;\land\;\left(\forall t\in\mathbb{N}:x^{t}\succsim y^{t}\right)\right]\implies x\succsim y$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is continuous
\end_layout

